  "narrative": "The twelve new results mainly strengthen the four central accepted associations as within-dataset, robustness-restricted comparisons rather than independent confirmations. For SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2 dependency, H104 shows the association remains very strong among TP53 wild-type cells (R54: +0.787, 95% CI 0.766 to 0.809), and H105 shows it persists in the lower-quality screen half (R55: +0.778, 0.751 to 0.805). These are not independent validations, but they argue against a simple explanation that the SMARCA2 effect is confined to TP53-loss cells or only to higher-quality screens. For KEAP1 loss/NFE2L2 dependency, H106 (R56: +0.798, 0.775 to 0.821 among SMARCA4 wild-type cells) and H107 (R57: +0.798, 0.770 to 0.827 in lower-quality screens) support robustness to SMARCA4 co-alteration status and screen-quality restriction. For MSI-high/WRN dependency, H108 (R58: +0.795, 0.762 to 0.828 among SMARCA4 wild-type cells) and H109 (R59: +0.790, 0.744 to 0.836 in lower-quality screens) are similarly strong; the exposed MSI-high cell in H109 is small but meets the cell-size rule. For TP53 wild-type/USP7 dependency, H110 (R60: +0.417, 0.338 to 0.496 among SMARCA4 wild-type cells) and H111 (R61: +0.360, 0.251 to 0.469 in lower-quality screens) remain far from zero. I accept and close H104-H111 as robustness-restricted dataset-level confirmations, not as causal or externally generalizable findings.\n\nThe four interaction tests are less supportive. H112, H113, and H114 test whether MSI-high or SMARCA4-loss states modify the main SMARCA2, NFE2L2, and WRN effects. The interaction estimates are small (R62: -0.017; R63: -0.026; R64: -0.022), their intervals include zero, and the upper bounds for clinically meaningful modification are modest. I reject these as unsupported effect-modification claims and close them. H115, USP7 modified by MYC amplification, has a larger point estimate (R65: +0.134) but a wide interval including zero (CI -0.048 to 0.315), likely due to the smaller MYC-amplified contrast cells; I leave it unresolved rather than rejecting. The main residual concern remains correlated co-alterations, unmeasured genomic context, screen artifacts, and discovery-sample overfitting; these new subsets reduce but do not eliminate that concern. Because H10 is the remaining central accepted association without direct independent validation and has now survived several robustness restrictions, I request independent validation for H10.",
