  "research_notes": "Updated interpretation: The four central accepted associations are now robust across co-alteration-excluded subsets and lower-quality-screen subsets. SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency is robust among TP53 wild-type and lower-quality screens and has independent validation. KEAP1 loss -> weaker/higher NFE2L2 dependency is robust among SMARCA4 wild-type and lower-quality screens and has Avana-subset independent validation. MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency is robust among SMARCA4 wild-type and lower-quality screens but still lacks direct independent validation; request validation for H10 now. TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency is robust among SMARCA4 wild-type and lower-quality screens and has direct independent validation plus high-mutation-burden validation. Interaction tests: no support that MSI-high modifies SMARCA2 or NFE2L2 effects, no support that SMARCA4 loss modifies WRN effect; USP7 x MYC amplification remains unresolved because estimate is positive but CI includes zero. Next focus: assess H10 validation, then consider remaining non-Avana library robustness and mutation-burden interactions, while keeping conclusions to within-dataset associations unless independent validation supports reproducibility.",
